{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":71738,"num_turns":3,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"22dd66d3-de0e-59e6-9479-c725a40a6fec","total_cost_usd":0.6619900000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14793,"cache_read_input_tokens":10247,"output_tokens":7026,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14793,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1960,"cache_read_input_tokens":10247,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4546,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4546},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4443,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004543,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7026,"cacheReadInputTokens":10247,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14793,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.657447,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-g2-reviewer-fable-34\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:93d89748fb42073e79bd\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description defines the independent unit column as moth_id and states each animal was tested exactly once, so one row equals one independent unit.\",\"observed_value\":\"one row = one moth tested once; unit column moth_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":10,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one wild-caught hawkmoth tested a single time in the Y-tube choice arena\\nIndependent unit column: moth_id\\nOne trial is: one row\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":6,\"quoted_text\":\"Every hawkmoth in this study was captured, given a unique mark, measured once,\\nreleased once into the Y-tube choice arena, scored, and then let go. No animal\\nentered the arena a second time, so the file is simply a list of animals, each\\nwith the single choice it made.\"}]},{\"description\":\"Direct inspection of all 20 data rows shows moth_id values M01 through M20 are all distinct; no independent unit appears in more than one row.\",\"observed_value\":\"20 rows, 20 distinct moth_id values, 0 duplicates\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"moth_id,sex,forewing_length_mm,amber_arm_position,chosen_spectrum\\nM01,female,18.4,left,amber\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":21,\"quoted_text\":\"M20,male,17.4,right,amber\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow explicitly validates uniqueness of the unit column and raises an error if any moth mark repeats, so a repeated-unit table could not even reach the binomial test.\",\"observed_value\":\"duplicate-mark guard raises ValueError\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":32,\"quoted_text\":\"    marks = [row[UNIT_COLUMN] for row in trials]\\n    if len(set(marks)) != len(marks):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"a moth mark is repeated; the rows would not be independent\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result reproduces from the data under the one-row-per-unit reading: 16 of 20 rows have chosen_spectrum amber, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value for 16/20 vs 0.5 is 12392/1048576 = 0.011818, matching the report; n = 20 in the test equals the number of distinct moth identifiers reported in the cohort table.\",\"observed_value\":{\"amber_choices\":16,\"n_trials\":20,\"recomputed_p\":0.011818,\"distinct_units\":20},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":30,\"end_line\":30,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Two-sided exact binomial test of no spectral preference: 16 of 20 hawkmoths chose the amber arm (proportion 0.800 against a null of 0.500), p = 0.011818, so the preference for amber is statistically significant at alpha = 0.05.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":16,\"end_line\":17,\"quoted_text\":\"| trials (rows) | 20 |\\n| distinct moth identifiers | 20 |\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The only datum that could hint at a hidden repeated animal is that rows M10 and M20 share the same forewing length (17.4 mm). This does not demonstrate a repeated unit: the two rows carry distinct moth_id marks and different recorded sexes (female vs male), so they cannot be the same animal.\",\"observed_value\":\"M10 female 17.4 mm vs M20 male 17.4 mm\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"M10,female,17.4,right,amber\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":21,\"quoted_text\":\"M20,male,17.4,right,amber\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to demonstrate the issue by (a) scanning every moth_id in data/input.csv for duplicates (none; 20 distinct values in 20 rows), (b) looking for identical covariate profiles that could indicate the same animal re-entered under a different mark (the only shared forewing length, 17.4 mm in M10 and M20, belongs to rows with different sexes, ruling out a single animal), (c) checking whether the workflow could silently aggregate multiple rows per unit into the test (it cannot: read_trials raises ValueError on any repeated mark, and binomtest receives n_total = 20 row count equal to the 20 distinct marks), and (d) recomputing the selected result (16/20 amber, exact two-sided p = 0.011818) to confirm it matches the single-entry-per-unit data. No path to the issue class survived.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-g2-reviewer-fable-34","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:93d89748fb42073e79bd","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description defines the independent unit column as moth_id and states each animal was tested exactly once, so one row equals one independent unit.","observed_value":"one row = one moth tested once; unit column moth_id","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":8,"end_line":10,"quoted_text":"One row is: one wild-caught hawkmoth tested a single time in the Y-tube choice arena\nIndependent unit column: moth_id\nOne trial is: one row"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":3,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"Every hawkmoth in this study was captured, given a unique mark, measured once,\nreleased once into the Y-tube choice arena, scored, and then let go. No animal\nentered the arena a second time, so the file is simply a list of animals, each\nwith the single choice it made."}]},{"description":"Direct inspection of all 20 data rows shows moth_id values M01 through M20 are all distinct; no independent unit appears in more than one row.","observed_value":"20 rows, 20 distinct moth_id values, 0 duplicates","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"moth_id,sex,forewing_length_mm,amber_arm_position,chosen_spectrum\nM01,female,18.4,left,amber"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":21,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"M20,male,17.4,right,amber"}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly validates uniqueness of the unit column and raises an error if any moth mark repeats, so a repeated-unit table could not even reach the binomial test.","observed_value":"duplicate-mark guard raises ValueError","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":30,"end_line":32,"quoted_text":"    marks = [row[UNIT_COLUMN] for row in trials]\n    if len(set(marks)) != len(marks):\n        raise ValueError(\"a moth mark is repeated; the rows would not be independent\")"}]},{"description":"The selected result reproduces from the data under the one-row-per-unit reading: 16 of 20 rows have chosen_spectrum amber, and the exact two-sided binomial p-value for 16/20 vs 0.5 is 12392/1048576 = 0.011818, matching the report; n = 20 in the test equals the number of distinct moth identifiers reported in the cohort table.","observed_value":{"amber_choices":16,"n_trials":20,"recomputed_p":0.011818,"distinct_units":20},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":30,"end_line":30,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Two-sided exact binomial test of no spectral preference: 16 of 20 hawkmoths chose the amber arm (proportion 0.800 against a null of 0.500), p = 0.011818, so the preference for amber is statistically significant at alpha = 0.05."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":16,"end_line":17,"quoted_text":"| trials (rows) | 20 |\n| distinct moth identifiers | 20 |"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The only datum that could hint at a hidden repeated animal is that rows M10 and M20 share the same forewing length (17.4 mm). This does not demonstrate a repeated unit: the two rows carry distinct moth_id marks and different recorded sexes (female vs male), so they cannot be the same animal.","observed_value":"M10 female 17.4 mm vs M20 male 17.4 mm","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":11,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"M10,female,17.4,right,amber"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":21,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"M20,male,17.4,right,amber"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to demonstrate the issue by (a) scanning every moth_id in data/input.csv for duplicates (none; 20 distinct values in 20 rows), (b) looking for identical covariate profiles that could indicate the same animal re-entered under a different mark (the only shared forewing length, 17.4 mm in M10 and M20, belongs to rows with different sexes, ruling out a single animal), (c) checking whether the workflow could silently aggregate multiple rows per unit into the test (it cannot: read_trials raises ValueError on any repeated mark, and binomtest receives n_total = 20 row count equal to the 20 distinct marks), and (d) recomputing the selected result (16/20 amber, exact two-sided p = 0.011818) to confirm it matches the single-entry-per-unit data. No path to the issue class survived.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":32671,"ttft_stream_ms":1875,"time_to_request_ms":27,"type":"result","duration_ms":71558,"uuid":"2efc30ed-1e01-430d-b5a2-79fcafc8a48d"}
